<<<
female, feminine, womanly. The fundamental difference between female & feminine is that
===
**female, feminine, womanly.** The fundamental difference between *female* & *feminine* is that
>>>

<<<
is idiomatic: female ruler & cook, but feminine rule & cookery; female attire, children, organs, but feminine gender, curtosity, arguments; & female & feminine education mean’ different things.
===
is idiomatic: *female ruler* & *cook*, but *feminine rule* & *cookery*; *female attire, children, organs*, but *feminine gender, curiosity, arguments*; & *female* & *feminine education* mean different things.
>>>

<<<
true that feminine is always to be preferred
===
true that *feminine* is always to be preferred
>>>

<<<
only, since female attire, female servant, are better than feminine attire & servant.
===
only, since *female attire, female servant*, are better than *feminine attire & servant*.
>>>

